    "text": "A conical portion of radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> and height&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> is removed from the bottom of a cylinder of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>. The volume of the remaining cylinder is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and its mass is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>. It is suspended by a string in a liquid of density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ρ</mi></math> where it stays vertical. The upper surface of the cylinder is at a depth&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></math> below the liquid surface. The force on the bottom of the cylinder by the liquid is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/136255.JPG\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 235px;\" />",
